 Modular status bar for dwm written in c.
 
+## wm session profile
+
+The local profile uses `wm-status` for keyboard, power profile, volume, battery,
+notification history/quiet status and the clock. dwm owns the bar/tray and
+statuscmd forwards block clicks. Power/battery clicks open Xfce Power Manager
+settings; the status process never applies automatic power policy. Notifications
+use Dunst's own history and pause state. Volume reuses wm-control.
+
+Each command has a coreutils timeout of six seconds plus a one-second kill grace.
+Reads are sequential: a slow command can delay other blocks up to that bound,
+not block the separate dwm process. Intervals and unique signal IDs are configured
+in config.h. The keyboard helper uses XKB. Runtime dependencies are packaged by
+the wm coordinator; this repository's Makefile builds only dwmblocks/wm-keyboard.
+
+The original project's notes and attribution follow.
+
